The method uses `Any` and `DateTime.Now`, so it returns true when only one reservation is valid and compares UTC expirations against local time, which contradicts the summary and can cause timezone bugs. Use `All` and `DateTime.UtcNow` to match the intended “every reservation is still valid” behavior.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;

public sealed class Basket
{
    public required IReadOnlyList<Reservation> Items { get; init; }

    /// <summary>True when every reservation in the basket is still valid.</summary>
    public bool IsStillValid()
    {
        return Items.All(item => item.ExpiresAtUtc > DateTime.UtcNow);
    }
}

public sealed record Reservation(string Sku, DateTime ExpiresAtUtc);
```

